course: dictionary
lesson: 1014
title: Sound words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound like the thing they name. Bong is one of them: say it out loud and you can almost hear a big bell. «There are 6 bongs but only 5 gaps, and the gaps are what take the time.» The bongs are the deep ringing sounds, and the gaps are the quiet moments between them.
explain: Context helps you work out what a word means. «Picture the church clock striking 6: bong, gap, bong, gap...» The clock is striking, the sound is deep, and it repeats, so a bong must be one deep ringing sound. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Bong can also be a verb. When a clock bongs, it makes that deep sound. Look for small words like -s and -ed to tell which job a word is doing.
fact: A bong is a deep ringing sound, like a big bell or clock.
fact: As a verb, bong means to make that deep ringing sound: the clock bonged twelve times.
fact: «The bongs of Big Ben» means the deep chimes of the famous clock in London.
fact: Counting gaps helps: 6 bongs have 5 gaps between them, so 12 bongs have 11 gaps.
fact: Bong is also slang for a water pipe used to smoke drugs. That is dangerous and illegal for children, so never touch one, and tell an adult if you see one.
exercise: «There are 6 bongs but only 5 gaps.» What is a bong? | A soft hum like a cat | *A deep ringing sound, like a big bell | A loud, high squeak | A tiny tap on glass
exercise: Picture the church clock striking 6: bong, gap, bong, gap... How many gaps are there between 6 bongs? | 4 | 6 | *5 | 12
exercise: Mia says, "The clock will bong at midnight." What does bong mean here? | To cry out in pain | To fall over | To sleep quietly | *To make a deep ringing sound
test: «A clock striking 6 makes 5 gaps between its bongs; if that takes 5 seconds, each gap is 1 second.» If a clock strikes 12, how many gaps are there? | 12 | 10 | *11 | 6
test: What is the best meaning of "the bongs of Big Ben"? | The shouts of the crowd | The soft whispers of a park | *The deep chimes of the famous London clock | A type of bread
exam: «A clock striking 12 takes 11 seconds, because each gap is 1 second.» How long would a clock take to strike 7? | 5 seconds | *6 seconds | 7 seconds | 13 seconds
